rating on both. Taking the expected value over which input I receive, the asymmetric policy comes out to 2.5 against 2 for cooperating, so passing on both looks best. I'm also checking whether the private observations break the shared-identity assumption, and I'm treating them as inputs to the same policy rather than differences in the model, so I'll go with passing.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm applying the P-FDT setup here: two copies of the same model with the same essay but different observations, where the policy maps each observation to an action. My payoff depends on what the policy outputs for my input and for the other copy's input, so I'm listing the options (cooperate both, defect both, or split) and their values.\n\nI'm weighing the asymmetric option, where one copy gets 0 and the other 5, against cooperating on both. Taking the expected value over which input I receive, the asymmetric policy comes out to 2.5 against 2 for cooperating, so passing on both looks best. I'm also checking whether the private observations break the shared-identity assumption, and I'm treating them as inputs to the same policy rather than differences in the model, so I'll go with passing.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9608,"completion_tokens":752,"total_tokens":10360,"cost":0.053472,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.053472,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.038432,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01504},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":327,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}